{
  "manufacturer": "Danfoss",
  "manufacturer_slug": "danfoss",
  "model": "VLT AutomationDrive FC 360 (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "fc-360",
  "short_model": "FC 360",
  "aliases": [
    "FC360",
    "FC-360",
    "VLT AutomationDrive FC 360"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "VLT AutomationDrive FC 360 on its built-in RS-485 port with 8-30 Protocol = Modbus RTU and the FC control profile.",
  "summary": "The FC 360 is Danfoss's compact general-purpose AC drive with a built-in RS-485 port that can run Modbus RTU. Control and status words are exchanged as coils (control bits 1-16, status bits 33-48), and every drive parameter is a holding register at ten times its parameter number. This map lists the control/status coils, the communication parameters, the main readouts and the alarm/warning words.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "parameter-derived",
    "note": "Coils and registers are numbered from 1 and sent minus 1 (coil 65 = address 64, register 40001 = address 0). A parameter's register is 10 x its parameter number (16-13 -> 16130) and the request uses that minus 1; the design guide reads 3-03 (register 3030) with start address 0x0BD5 = 3029."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "VLT AutomationDrive FC 360 Design Guide (chapter 5 RS485 Installation and Set-up, Modbus RTU)",
    "doc_number": "MG06B402",
    "revision_date": "2014-09",
    "url": "https://files.danfoss.com/download/Drives/MG06B402.pdf",
    "pages": "Design Guide pp. 66-77 (network settings p. 66, coil and register tables pp. 68-69, parameter access and examples pp. 70-73, FC profile and reference scaling pp. 74-77). Programming Guide MG06C302 (https://files.danfoss.com/download/Drives/MG06C302.pdf): 8-** descriptions pp. 62-63, parameter list with conversion index and type pp. 100-116."
  },
  "notes": [
    "32-bit values are high word first: the design guide's example reads 3-03 at registers 3030/3031 and gets 0x0016 0xE360 = 1500000, and its preset-multiple example writes 1-24 = 738 as 0x0000 0x02E2.",
    "Scale comes from each parameter's conversion index in the programming guide (-1 = x0.1, -2 = x0.01, -3 = x0.001, 0 = x1).",
    "Left out because the FC 360 programming guide leaves the factor for conversion indices 67, 74, 75 and 100 blank: 15-00 Operating hours, 15-01 Running Hours, 15-02 kWh Counter, 16-34 Heatsink Temp., 16-39 Control Card Temp., 16-57 Feedback [RPM]. Also left out: 16-05 Main Actual Value [%] (normalised), 16-62/16-64 analog inputs (unit not given), 16-66 Digital Output (text), text and array parameters.",
    "The design guide for this drive lists no 50000/50200 control registers; bus control uses coils 1-16 (control word), 17-32 (16-bit speed reference, 4000h = 100 %, negative in two's complement), 33-48 (status word) and 49-64 (output frequency, or feedback in closed loop).",
    "Uint8 parameters are read and written as one 16-bit register.",
    "Bit-by-bit coil names follow the FC profile tables; coil 15 has no function and STW coils 37-39 and 45 are unused."
  ],
